When I receive a new dataset, I first try to understand what the data contains and how it is structured. Then I check the tables, columns, keys and relationships between them
--Check tables,total columns in each table, data type in each column and column name in each table
SELECT
    TABLE_SCHEMA,
    TABLE_NAME,
    ORDINAL_POSITION,
    COLUMN_NAME,
    DATA_TYPE,
    CHARACTER_MAXIMUM_LENGTH,
    NUMERIC_PRECISION,
    NUMERIC_SCALE,
    IS_NULLABLE,
    COUNT(*) OVER(PARTITION BY TABLE_SCHEMA, TABLE_NAME) AS TotalColumns
FROM INFORMATION_SCHEMA.COLUMNS
ORDER BY TABLE_SCHEMA, TABLE_NAME, ORDINAL_POSITION;

